preConditionHook:
// THE TREND HAS ALREADY MADE MORE THAN maxLegs SAME-DIRECTION PUSHES since the
// last opposite-direction leg -- after which Grimes says the probability of
// pullback failure rises with every further leg (G05-17). His threshold is
// three, the default. Expected use is NEGATED, as a block on further
// with-trend entries; the corpus states every "do not trade while X" claim
// positively and lets the per-placement negate toggle give the block.
//
// THE COUNT IS A RUN, NOT A SLOT SCAN, and that is what makes the rule
// reachable. The merge note warned that decision 14's newest-first scan keeps
// only three pivots per series, so "more than three" looked unreachable. It is
// not, once the chain is tested AS THE SCAN GOES -- HigherSwingLowRun's `legs`
// construction: walk the window newest-first, and for each newly found swing
// high compare it with the previously found (NEWER) one; while the chain of
// higher highs holds, count a push; the first break of the chain closes the
// count. No pivot slots, no array, and maxLegs is unbounded above. The only
// limit is pivotLookback, the window the pushes must fit inside.
//
// MIRRORED, NOT IDENTICAL, a DELIBERATE DEPARTURE from the merged slice's
// `sides: same`. "The trend has made more than maxLegs same-direction pushes"
// is a directional claim: a long placement wants the count of UP pushes (the
// chain of higher swing highs) and a short placement the count of DOWN pushes
// (lower swing lows). Copying one side into the other would block long entries
// because the DOWNtrend is extended, which is not what the source says. The
// identical-text reading is reachable anyway by placing the rule twice.
//
// PUSHES ARE COUNTED AS COMPARISONS: a chain of four higher highs is three
// pushes, so maxLegs 3 fires on the fourth confirmed higher high. Same
// convention as HigherSwingLowRun's `legs` (legs - 1 comparisons).
//
// NOT LegCountAtLeast, whose counter runs over the legs of the CURRENT
// PULLBACK off the settled bar counter -- a different series and a different
// reset. Not ThreePushPattern, the fixed-count sibling at exactly three pivots,
// which tests three pivot PRICES rather than counting an open-ended run. Not
// HigherSwingLowRun at a large `legs`, which asks whether a run of exactly `legs`
// pivots is rising -- a floor stated as an ALL-OF, where this counts the run
// and compares the count.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED (merge decision 14) and the chain is tested inside
// it, so no Occurrence 3+ call is made -- that row is UNMEASURED. MEASURED
// (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot bar is AT
// OR BEYOND the swingStrength OLDER bars and STRICTLY BEYOND the swingStrength
// NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER kk the newer bar, so the
// strict half is the kk < jj loop; the confirmation lag is exactly
// swingStrength bars, so jj starts there; candidate offsets run 0..Length-1
// inclusive so jj stops at pivotLookback - 1, while the neighbourhood test
// reaches swingStrength bars PAST the window -- deepest bar touched
// pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12
// relational tolerance; the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the measured
// high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists, so plain EL governs. Written
// WITHOUT break, matching the twin statement for statement.
//
// hiPrev / loPrev are only ever READ once the count has reached 2, which is
// exactly when they were written earlier on the same bar -- never a sentinel,
// never a stale price, and never compared against -1. The chain flags are what
// stop a later pivot being folded into the run.
//
// Every scratch value that must survive the bar is a localVariables entry
// rather than a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement; the loop counters and per-candidate flags are block-scoped.
//
// Deepest bar touched: pivotLookback - 1 + swingStrength.
pivS = (int)swingStrength;
pivW = (int)pivotLookback;
nHi = 0;
nLo = 0;
hiPrev = 0.0;
loPrev = 0.0;
upRun = 0;
dnRun = 0;
upChain = true;
dnChain = true;
for (int jj = pivS; jj <= pivW - 1; ++jj) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int kk = jj - pivS; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + pivS; ++kk) {
        if (!el_ge(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi) {
        nHi = nHi + 1;
        if (nHi >= 2 && upChain && el_gt(hiPrev, high[jj])) {
            upRun = upRun + 1;
        }
        if (nHi >= 2 && upChain && el_le(hiPrev, high[jj])) {
            upChain = false;
        }
        hiPrev = high[jj];
    }
    if (okLo) {
        nLo = nLo + 1;
        if (nLo >= 2 && dnChain && el_lt(loPrev, low[jj])) {
            dnRun = dnRun + 1;
        }
        if (nLo >= 2 && dnChain && el_ge(loPrev, low[jj])) {
            dnChain = false;
        }
        loPrev = low[jj];
    }
}
